<title>USA: InControl METRIX gets FDA clearance.</title>
<headline>InControl METRIX gets FDA clearance.</headline>
<dateline>REDMOND, Wash 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>InControl Inc said it received U.S. Food and Drug Administration clearance to expand the clinical trial of its METRIX implantable atrial defibrillation system.</p>
<p>The announcement follows the successful conclusion of the initial safety study, which was conducted at five U.S. hospitals.  The FDA's clearance for clinical trial expansion will make InControl's METRIX device available for implantation at 25 U.S. hospitals.  The clearance for expansion will also allow physicians to begin to use the METRIX System's patient-activated therapy option.</p>
</text>
